# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform, so that a Windows runner,
# a Linux runner and a developer test the same bytes (CIC-11 of the PowerShell standards).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The three scripts whose text the validation kit joins with CRLF, uploads to Intune, or hashes
# on the lab device are checked out with CRLF on every platform, as a Windows checkout had them
# before this file existed, so that a round sends the same bytes wherever it is started from.
# The kit's other scripts that are delivered to a device, such as New-IslHarnessUser.ps1, are LF
# like the rest: they are sent as they are, and nothing depends on their line endings.
Validation/Fixtures.ps1 text eol=crlf
Validation/Probe.ps1 text eol=crlf
Validation/Win32Install.ps1 text eol=crlf
